SPRD PCIe: retain the blocking allocation semantics of iommu_map on Linux 6.6.

sprd_pcie_iommu_init is called directly from PCI probe before driver spinlocks.
The old five-argument iommu_map used GFP_KERNEL internally; Linux 6.3 exposes
that allocation flag in its public API. No kernel Kconfig symbols are changed.

References:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.2/drivers/iommu/iommu.c
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.3/drivers/iommu/iommu.c

--- a/package/mtk/applications/5g-modem/quectel_SRPD_PCIE/src/pcie/sprd_pcie_ep_device.c
+++ b/package/mtk/applications/5g-modem/quectel_SRPD_PCIE/src/pcie/sprd_pcie_ep_device.c
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@
 			dev_info(dev, "sprd_pcie_iommu_init iova:%d have been used", (u32)addr);
 			continue;
 		}
-		ret = iommu_map(domain, addr, addr, pg_size, IOMMU_READ | IOMMU_WRITE);
+		ret = iommu_map(domain, addr, addr, pg_size, IOMMU_READ | IOMMU_WRITE, GFP_KERNEL);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_info(dev, "sprd_pcie_iommu_init iommu_map failed");
 			return;
